CORE
main.sh
--shell-max-string-length 30
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[assertion\.1\] file main.sh line 3 .*: SUCCESS$
^\[assertion\.2\] file main.sh line 4 .*: SUCCESS$
^\[assertion\.3\] file main.sh line 5 .*: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
shell-string-length
--
Inputs are at most --shell-max-string-length bytes; strings that the
script builds are not bounded.
